  "title": "elasticsearch: versions are really unsigned, fix format truncation",
  "description": "Elasticsearch is written in Java, so its ints (stored as varints)\nare all signed. The version number is really unsigned (and the\nsigned bit should never be set anyway.) It's already added to the\ntree cast as unsigned. Store it that way as well, so that when\nperforming div and mod to extract the components the result is\nalways non-negative (C and its silly truncated division).\n\nThis has the benefit of preventing format truncation warnings.\n\nPing #20175",
